# [FABLE-5] sq-hmd7l.10 — vendored ORE-style CONSISTENCY task (expected: INCONSISTENT).
# Hand-authored, hand-verified. The clash is DERIVED, not asserted (non-vacuous: the
# ABox seed contains no direct contradiction, so the seed-clash shortcut cannot fire and
# the tableau must actually run): a ∀ on the SUPER-role s constrains an edge asserted on
# the SUB-role r, forcing b ∈ B, which clashes with the asserted b ∈ C under
# disjoint(B, C). A tableau that dropped ∀-propagation through the subPropertyOf
# hierarchy — or disjointness — would wrongly report consistent.
@prefix : <http://sparq.dev/bench/ore-smoke/role-disjoint#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

:r rdfs:subPropertyOf :s .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :s ; owl:allValuesFrom :B ] .
:B owl:disjointWith :C .

:a a :A .
:a :r :b .
:b a :C .
